you can use custom dashboards to tailor  the monitoring experience to your  environment to create your first custom  dashboard click dashboards at the top of  the screen and create here we'll add  three charts to our new dashboard first  I'll choose a resource type of Google  App Engine module and then I'll I'll  search for latency metrics here I'll add  the response latency x' 95th percentile  so now I have a chart that displays the  95th percentile latency for each of my  App Engine modules I'll let a second  chart for the App Engine responses for  each of the modules so again I'll type  responses to filter the list and then  I'll choose total responses and click  Save and I'll add a third chart for  Google compute engine instances in this  case I'm primarily interested in CPU  usage for each of my instances and I'll  click Save so now I have three charts on  my custom dashboard I can also change  the layout of that dashboard perhaps I  want to view it in a three column view I  can also rearrange the charts on the  dashboard by clicking on any of the  titles and moving it in into its  location if I want to look at the  dashboard in full-screen mode I can  click the fullscreen icon in the top  right hand corner of the screen this is  particularly useful for viewing the  dashboard on a large LED screen in an  office to the left of the fullscreen  icon you can access the settings for the  chart such as the setting to show all of  the legends on the charts and to the  left of that I can choose to enable auto  refresh for my charts and then if I  zoomed in any of the charts to a  particular time frame I can always use  the reset zoom icon to reset the time  frame  all of my charts and then finally if I  wanted to choose a specific time frame  for the charts I can click on any of the  links in the top right hand corner to  view that time frame here I'm looking at  a day's worth of data across all of my  charts and so those are the core  capabilities of the custom dashboard  feature there are many more capabilities  for you to take advantage of as you  familiarize yourself with custom  dashboards
 

